          },
          "mechanism": "Body weight (combined with height to form BMI) confounds the exposure-outcome relationship.",
          "justification": "Obesity is associated with symptom severity in perimenopause (and thus with hormone use initiation); obesity also directly affects cholesterol levels. Estrogen metabolism is altered by adiposity, and adipose tissue produces endogenous estrogen. Will be combined with height variables to calculate BMI.",
          "role": "confounder",
          "proxy_for": null,
          "contestable": false
        },
        {
