          "mechanism": "Smoking history confounds the relationship between hormone use and cholesterol diagnosis.",
          "justification": "Smokers have elevated cardiovascular risk and abnormal lipid profiles; smoking is also associated with different patterns of healthcare engagement and symptom attribution that may affect both hormone use and cholesterol screening/diagnosis.",
          "role": "confounder",
