          },
          "mechanism": "Type 1 diabetes is a descendant of exposure and mediator of the exposure-outcome relationship.",
          "justification": "Estrogen affects glucose metabolism; type 1 diabetes diagnosis by a healthcare provider is a marker of medical surveillance and healthcare engagement, which affects the likelihood of cholesterol screening and diagnosis. Adjusting for diabetes would block the pathway from estrogen use → metabolic changes → cholesterol diagnosis awareness.",
          "role": "mediator",
          "proxy_for": null,
          "contestable": false
        },
