          },
          "mechanism": "Hypertension is a mediator of the exposure-outcome relationship and marker of healthcare engagement.",
          "justification": "Estrogen affects blood pressure regulation; unopposed estrogen may increase hypertension risk. Hypertension diagnosis, once made, increases medical surveillance and increases the likelihood of cholesterol screening and diagnosis being documented. Adjusting for hypertension would block the indirect pathway from hormone use → hypertension → increased healthcare engagement → cholesterol diagnosis.",
          "role": "mediator",
          "proxy_for": null,
          "contestable": false
        },
